\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Global proof DAG. Public textbook data enter only at [1]. Nodes [2]--[6] generate the total graphs, source algebra, compactification, target quotient, and total shell graph. Its ordinary value gives unit progress at [7], while every boundary value enters [14]. Thus [8] forces aligned support. Nodes [9]--[11] close the divergent-price branch. Every ordinary or graph-boundary value also enters [14]; finite price joins it at [15]. The generated zero-price equations at [16] feed finite-depth viability pruning at [17]. A generated finite rational-cylinder transcript gives [12]. Failure of every finite pruning depth constructs the path and stationary mechanism at [18]. No live node is an unexpanded analytic label.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
